Well, actually no - not e-mail.  I've sent out enough form letters in the
last few days to people who have requested e-mail copies of the spoilers.

We (the spoiler dev team) have a policy of not sending out e-mail copies
of the spoilers (we get and send out enough mail anyways).  However...

Bill Randle, the moderator of comp.sources.games currently has a copy of
revision 5.35 of the spoilers, and will be posting those to comp.sources.games
shortly, so you should be able to grab them off of there.

Once they've been posted there, we will be posting a list of ftp, uucp, and
e-mail sites where you can get them from, so be on the lookout for that if
you don't have access to comp.sources.games.

>in future distributions, help documentation should be conveniently
>packaged with the game!  its so simple and really counts for a lot.

I'm currently working on an *unofficial* patch to the nethack code that
will allow nethackers to access the spoiler file directly from within
nethack by using the '?' command.  It will probably be released with the
next revision.

>now if we could just get the "/" command to be really descriptive ...

We're also working on creating updated monster descriptions for each and
every individual monster within the game.  Hopefully we'll be able to get
the dev team to include these into the official code.

